<title>SWEDEN: FORECAST-Scania 1996 profit 43 pct lower.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Scania 1996 profit 43 pct lower.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish truck maker Scania is expected to post a profit of 2.76 billion crowns after financial items for 1996 compared to 4.85 billion in 1995, a poll by Reuters of 16 analysts showed on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Forecasts ranged from 2.46 billion crowns to 3.20 billion.</p>
<p>The average of 14 analysts' forecasts put earnings per share at 9.52 crowns compared to 16.40 a year earlier.</p>
<p>The same number of analysts' forecasts put the consensus dividend forecast at 5.6 crowns.</p>
<p>Scania is due to publish its report on February 18.</p>
<p>Analysts that participated in the poll were from Kleinwort Benson, Swedbank, Fischer Partners, James Capel, Morgan Grenfell, Fiba Nordic, Handelsbanken, Nordiska, Foreningsbanken, Aros, CSFB, Enskilda, Den Danske Bank, Ohman, Carnegie, Aragon.</p>
<p>PROFIT AFTER FIN ITEMS (MLN SKR)</p>
<p>			  AVG	     RANGE     ANALYSTS</p>
<p>  1996		  2,759	   2,400-3,200	 16</p>
<p>  1997		  3,764	   3,265-4,641	 15</p>
<p>  1998		  4,466	   3,320-5,639	 13</p>
<p> Profit/shr 1996 (SKR) 9.52	 8.50-11.40	  14</p>
<p> Profit/shr 1997	13.47	11.60-16.40	  14</p>
<p> Profit/shr 1998	15.93	12.00-20.10	  14</p>
<p> Dividend 1996 (SKR)   5.61	 4.00-6.25	   14</p>
<p> Dividend 1997	   6.64	 4.00-8.00	   12</p>
<p> Dividend 1998	   7.37	 4.50-8.50	   11</p>
<p>-- Henrik Alberius, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1250</p>
